#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lb-board: a Plane board for a GitHub repository, whatever the team's workflow. Lunabee internal.

Extracted from whackagent's wa-backlog (Plane board only). Projects vendor it as is (`.lunabee/board/lb-board`); the
"Lunabee Plane board" GitHub App receiver runs `lb-board hook` on every push and pull request event, from the
default branch. Python 3.9+ stdlib plus `gh`.

Ticket = Plane work item, id = its key "CUM-12". A branch or PR belongs to the ticket whose key it names anywhere
(`feature/CUM-12-login`, `cum-12`), else to the one card linked in the PR body. Settings come from the repo
variables PLANE_* (`provision` writes them); the Plane API key from env PLANE_API_KEY only.

States: todo → grilling (claim) → grilled (spec pushed) → coding (claim) → review (PR opened) → done (PR merged),
plus canceled. Claims are git refs refs/lb-claims/<key>/<phase> on the GitHub repo: atomic, one holder. Priority =
card order. Sprint = a parent card labeled lb-sprint plus a cycle of the same name; milestone = a module;
dependency = a "blocked by" relation. whackagent (rlatapy-luna/whackagent) runs its Plane board on this script.

Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 error · 2 usage · 3 claim taken · 4 wrong state for the operation.
"""

